Z||000000||Jncomutt||07-08-2001||01:20 AM||||Whats the best plug to use for my 84 2M4.  Car has just over 53k mi. on it and it seems like it could have a bit smoother idle and gas mileage.  When I did a search, it seemed the rapidfire or splitfire were the way to go.  Anyone have info on this?<P>Oh yea, and I'm planning to switch to a MSD blaster coil & the 6a ignition thingy there..   Any opinions or recommandations?  Thanx again!||||reg||1
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-08-2001||06:23 AM||||I never used Rapidfire on my 4cyl, but I'll tell you now that the splitfire are a waste of money.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SigPic.jpg">  <BR>AIM - DecadenceR<BR>"For though I cannot fly, I'm not content to crawl..."||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||07-08-2001||09:42 AM||||Personally, I'd try the Bosch Platinum+4 plug...four ground electrodes and center electrode that are platinum.<P>Looks like it would provide plenty of spark with just about zero potential for misfire. Platinum plugs also foul less than regular plugs...important in the 2.5 since most have valve seals that let oil into the combustion chamber at startup.<P>Probably also a good choice as your's isn't a 87+ DIS motor.||||reg||1
