Z||000013||DecadenceR||07-09-2001||01:16 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrgone:<BR><B>i heard that the material platinum has a problem with some fieros.. i forget why..<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The DIS Fieros don't do well with the Bosch +4 because the electrode is pretty much even with the ceramic. The DIS kinda eats it up for some reason, I'm not sure why, and erodes the electrode until it's so far inside the ceramic, it doesn't produce very well.||||reg||1
Z||000014||rogergarrison||07-09-2001||07:35 PM||||ive always used Bosch Platinum with single electrode and theyve worked fine. the multi tips are pretty worthless since the spark will only go across the best one of the four anyway. I am tuning mine up today for a road trip to the Vintage Races in Pittsburg and trying AC Delcos for a change/ comparison.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||kslish||07-09-2001||10:32 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rogergarrison:<BR><B>I am tuning mine up today for a road trip to the Vintage Races in Pittsburg and trying AC Delcos for a change/ comparison.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Roger, are you referring to the Pgh. Vintage Grand Prix on July 21st-22nd?  There is a car show on the 21st at Schenley Park right off the site of the road race course.  You are welcome to join me and the West Penn Fiero Club in our cookout on the showfield with the Pittsburgh Thunderbird Club for lunch on the 21st.<P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000016||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||07-09-2001||10:43 PM||||plugs are plugs.  I find the autolite plugs to be a good value, but the delco rapid fires are nice too.<P>Currently I am running Autolite platinums with good results.  But, expecting a spark plug to increase the power of your Fiero is unreasonable unless your current plugs are shot.<P>Cheap plugs may not be plated.  In this case, removing them later on may not be easy.  Since their threads are plated, the platinum plugs can be a better choice in the long run.<P>Otherwise, unless it's a sh*tfire, a plug is a plug.<P>||||reg||1
