Z||000018||stsmithgt||07-10-2001||01:56 PM||||I've had the platinum +4's in my V-6 and I wasn't impressed.  I remeber we used to mark our plugs so we could make sure the spark was facing the cylinder(not being blocked by the electroed).  It's one of those details that doesn't do much to a stock street car.  <BR>I had a chevy 283 with 11.5:1 pop-up pistons bored 125 thousanths over back in high school and the little details like that gave you something to talk about.||||reg||1
